### Page 15 of 15

```text
13

The capital budget was presented to the Board at the March 2023 meeting and has
been adjusted to accommodate the overall budget.

Items marked with * indicate projects that we will continue to collect funds (CFCs and
6th Penny) over several years but will be required to fund through reserves in the
current FY.  For the terminal parking lot, approximately $823,361 will be collected
using 6th penny funds.  Based on our current collection rate, the funds will be fully
recovered in four years.  For the rental car lot, the budgeted about of $829,075 will be
collected in 11 years based on our current collection rate.

Cash Balance Forecast
As of April 15, 2023, the Board has $6,035,389 in cash reserves.  Of that, $1,030,815
is currently restricted in investments.  As indicated in the overall budget on page 6,
approximately $3,082,264 will need to come from reserves or debt services. At this
time, the Airport has no outstanding debt service. Of that amount, $697,217 is
required to be paid for capital projects for our local match.

If using available cash reserves, the projected remaining cash balance at the end of
FY 2024 would be $2,953,125.
```
